{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1780452453,"nonce":"2SQxmHFXcl/J0RCKMiEhhsZmKQY=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABEMUM1Q","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/209","origin":"github"},"title":"Record operator command inputs (marine/command, manual/helm) in the boat-side bag","message":"The boat-side bag recorder (`bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat.yaml`, `/**/logger` allowlist) records command **results/status** — `marine/response`, `marine/status/mission_manager`, `run_tasks`/`follow_path` action status, `piloting_mode/autonomous/cmd_vel` — but **not the raw operator command inputs**:\n\n- `/bizzy/marine/command` — the operator goto/hover/mission/standby command bus\n- `/bizzy/piloting_mode/manual/helm` — manual teleop + takeover events\n\nBoth exist boat-side (the boat's mission_manager and piloting mux consume them, bridged from the operator station) and are low-rate (46 and ~5.7k msgs over a ~2.7 h run — trivial size).\n\n## Why it matters\nToday the only record of *what was commanded* (and the manual-takeover timeline) lives in the **operator-station bag**. The #205 wrap-up needed that operator bag to confirm the boat was never sped up (13:36) and to time the 15:27 takeover — the boat-side bag alone couldn't answer. If the operator bag is lost, the boat (the system of record) can't reconstruct the commands. Recording them boat-side makes the boat bag self-contained.\n\n## Fix\nAdd both topics to the `/**/logger` `record.topics` list in `bizzyboat.yaml`.\n\n## Open / to verify\n- **IzzyBoat parallel:** `izzyboat_project11/config/izzyboat.yaml` likely has the same gap — fold into this PR (fleet consistency) or handle separately? (surfacing, not deferring silently)\n- **Pre-merge:** verify both topics actually resolve on gabby (bridged, exact names) before trusting the recorder captures them.\n\nFound during the #205 wrap-up (rolker/unh_echoboats_project11#205).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}